# Pi recordings: external SSD only

- All Pi recording data (dashboard Dataset recording, `record_session.sh`, `pi_mic_check.py`, service `TAP_DIR`) is stored **only** in `/mnt/sonitude-drive/sonitude-recordings/` (Samsung T5, exFAT, fstab UUID `B424-9B8F`). `~/sb_rt_dev/measure` is a symlink to it.
- The drive also holds the owner's **personal files**. Agents must never list in detail, read, write, move, rename or delete anything outside `sonitude-recordings/`.
- Never record to the SD card. Scripts refuse if `/mnt/sonitude-drive` isn't mounted; keep that guard.
- Mounting, unmounting and fstab are owner (sudo) actions.
- Reference: `docs/pi_dashboard_models_and_recording_20261105.md`.
